### Tone: End-of-game award: Optimist, the player who guessed too high most often (at least three times, two answers
### in three). $count: those answers. The world is smaller than they think; gently patronising.

award-optimist-1 =
    The Optimist award goes to { $name }: too high { $count ->
        [one] once.
       *[other] { $count } times.
    } You believe in big numbers. Big numbers do not believe in you.
award-optimist-2 = { $name }, you overestimate everything. It must be a lovely way to live. Inaccurate, but lovely.
award-optimist-3 = Optimist: { $name }. In your world, everything is larger, longer and more numerous. Reality disagrees, politely.
award-optimist-4 = { $name } aimed high, every time. The truth was lower, every time. Somebody had to tell you.
award-optimist-5 =
    { $count ->
        [one] One answer
       *[other] { $count } answers
    } too high from { $name }. Your glass is not half full. It is overflowing, and wrong.
award-optimist-6 = The award for thinking big goes to { $name }. Big, and then a bit bigger. Then a bit more.
award-optimist-7 = Optimist: { $name }. If you ever estimate your own bill at a restaurant, please don’t.
award-optimist-8 = { $name }, consistently too high. I suspect you round up as a lifestyle.
award-optimist-9 = The Optimist goes to { $name }, who sees the world through magnifying glasses.
award-optimist-10 = { $name }, the most generous estimator in the room. Generous to the numbers. Not to your score.
